        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nx9Qj4Xa0HHLW7jD4z0X-78" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="=deleting key after some time" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="480" y="-970" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label=". For Android I want to go native, and publish on fdroid. That gives me free hosting, reproducible builds, and credibility.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;2. For ios i have to do pwa. Melle has a https webserver, with a bit of luck he is willing to run a script that pulls the code from some git server, build it, and host it.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;3. I don&#39;t know about languages. Rust sounds good, maybe go.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;4. For debugging, I want a linux native app, so I can do extensive logging and stepping through code.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;5. For debugging, I want a Wireshark plug-in that understands the protocol.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;6 for debugging, I want to re-find the program that can show me crypto calculations step by step&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;7. I want to make github actions that first do tests, and if everything is good, then build the android app, the linux app, and the pwa&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;8. I need to write out who is encrypting, who is signing. And who is storing what, and for how long.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;9. I need to build anti spam, so a user can only create so.many groups per day. This requires consensus on the network about the current time, so it also works when the local clock is not synchronized with the real time.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;10. I need to have some mechanism for two nodes doing stuff at the same time. Especially conflicting stuff&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;11. I need some mechanism to forget about inactive users. For instance remove a member that has not played for 18 months.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;12 I need a good ui for doing the invite/request thing using qr codes. Signal sucks in this regard.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;13. I need a way to initially distribute a list of relayservers for setting up the webrtc connections. And have a qr and copy-paste fallback when all relayservers are gone.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;14. I need something that can distribute a database of groups, and keep it updated when a new group appears.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;15. The schedule of games also needs to be distributed.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;16. A mechanism to make and remove administrators per groups, and what they can do. The same for members and players.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;17 a way to capture who is bringing required items, like a ball, keys, bibs, cones, ball pump, extra water, the group flag, and so on.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;18 we need a logo for the app&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;19 we need a logo for Terrible Football Haarlem.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;20 we need to draw/find the rest of the logos in the app.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;21 Everybody is allowed to create new categories, sports and groups. This needs to be protected against spamming, users should ignore/favored them, and they have to auto-dissapear when they are not used.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;22. A parental control, where children can&#39;t search or join new groups, and can&#39;t chat, so only state they are going to a game.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;23. The discipline to make a minimal version first, that has none of the above, and can only be used to show if you are going to the game.&#xa;40m" link=". For Android I want to go native, and publish on fdroid. That gives me free hosting, reproducible builds, and credibility.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;2. For ios i have to do pwa. Melle has a https webserver, with a bit of luck he is willing to run a script that pulls the code from some git server, build it, and host it.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;3. I don&#39;t know about languages. Rust sounds good, maybe go.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;4. For debugging, I want a linux native app, so I can do extensive logging and stepping through code.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;5. For debugging, I want a Wireshark plug-in that understands the protocol.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;6 for debugging, I want to re-find the program that can show me crypto calculations step by step&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;7. I want to make github actions that first do tests, and if everything is good, then build the android app, the linux app, and the pwa&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;8. I need to write out who is encrypting, who is signing. And who is storing what, and for how long.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;9. I need to build anti spam, so a user can only create so.many groups per day. This requires consensus on the network about the current time, so it also works when the local clock is not synchronized with the real time.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;10. I need to have some mechanism for two nodes doing stuff at the same time. Especially conflicting stuff&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;11. I need some mechanism to forget about inactive users. For instance remove a member that has not played for 18 months.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;12 I need a good ui for doing the invite/request thing using qr codes. Signal sucks in this regard.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;13. I need a way to initially distribute a list of relayservers for setting up the webrtc connections. And have a qr and copy-paste fallback when all relayservers are gone.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;14. I need something that can distribute a database of groups, and keep it updated when a new group appears.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;15. The schedule of games also needs to be distributed.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;16. A mechanism to make and remove administrators per groups, and what they can do. The same for members and players.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;17 a way to capture who is bringing required items, like a ball, keys, bibs, cones, ball pump, extra water, the group flag, and so on.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;18 we need a logo for the app&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;19 we need a logo for Terrible Football Haarlem.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;20 we need to draw/find the rest of the logos in the app.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;21 Everybody is allowed to create new categories, sports and groups. This needs to be protected against spamming, users should ignore/favored them, and they have to auto-dissapear when they are not used.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;22. A parental control, where children can&#39;t search or join new groups, and can&#39;t chat, so only state they are going to a game.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;23. The discipline to make a minimal version first, that has none of the above, and can only be used to show if you are going to the game.&#xa;40m" id="oP1f0DHWsyw6lLXi408K-1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="1230" width="560" x="-660" y="930" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
